<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Work room by room and top to bottom, so dust falls onto areas you haven't cleaned yet.</li><li>Declutter before you clean; it makes every other job quicker.</li><li>Prioritise the kitchen, bathroom and anywhere winter condensation has left mould.</li><li>Spread the checklist over several days rather than trying to do it all at once.</li><li>Book specialist jobs like carpets and ovens separately if you'd rather not tackle them.</li></ul></div>
<h2>Before you start: how to plan your spring clean</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Declutter first.</strong> Clear surfaces, sort cupboards and bag up donations. Cleaning around clutter takes much longer.</li>
<li><strong>Gather your supplies.</strong> Microfibre cloths, a multi-purpose cleaner, a descaler, a degreaser, glass cleaner, a mop, a hoover with attachments, rubber gloves and a step stool. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:eco-friendly-cleaning-products}}">eco-friendly cleaning products</a> explains which gentler options actually work.</li>
