		'faqs'        => [
			[ 'Does vinegar remove limescale?', 'Yes. White vinegar is a mild acid that dissolves limescale on taps, shower heads and kettles. Leave it to soak, scrub gently, then rinse well, and don’t use it on natural stone.' ],
			[ 'Is the water in Hull hard?', 'Much of Hull and East Yorkshire has hard water, which is why limescale builds up so quickly. You can check the hardness for your address by entering your postcode on your water supplier’s website.' ],
