	[
		'slug'        => 'cleaning-before-selling-your-house',
		'title'       => 'Cleaning Before Selling Your House: Tips to Impress Buyers',
		'seo_title'   => 'Cleaning Before Selling Your House: Tips to Impress Buyers',
		'description' => 'Cleaning before selling your house? Our room-by-room tips cover photos, viewings, smells and kitchens, so buyers see a well-cared-for home from the start.',
		'category'    => 'home-cleaning',
		'service'     => 'one-off-cleaning',
		'related'     => [ 'moving-house-cleaning-timeline', 'kitchen-deep-clean-checklist', 'deep-clean-vs-regular-clean' ],
		'image'       => 'staged home interior',
		'excerpt'     => 'How to clean and present your home before the listing photos and viewings, with a quick routine to keep it ready while you sell.',
		'content'     => <<<'HTML'
<p>Cleaning before selling your house is one of the simplest ways to make a strong first impression. Deep clean before the estate agent takes photos, focusing on the kitchen, bathrooms, entrance, windows and any smells, then keep a quick routine going so the home is ready for every viewing.</p>
<p>Buyers can't see your home's history, only what's in front of them. Clean grout, clear worktops and fresh-smelling rooms suggest a house that's been looked after; limescale, dusty skirting boards and a greasy hob make people wonder what else has been neglected.</p>
<p>Here's how to get your home ready to sell, from decluttering through to the final checks before buyers arrive, with practical notes for homes in Hull and East Yorkshire.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Declutter first, then deep clean before the listing photos are taken.</li><li>Kitchens, bathrooms and the entrance make the strongest impression on buyers.</li><li>Deal with smells at the source rather than covering them up.</li><li>A short routine before each viewing keeps the house looking its best throughout the sale.</li></ul></div>
<h2>Why cleaning matters when you sell a house</h2>
<p>Most buyers see your home online first, and photos pick up more than you'd expect: smears on mirrors, limescale on taps, scuffs on walls. A clean, bright home photographs better and gives people a reason to book a viewing.</p>
<p>In person, buyers notice the details. A spotless home won't add a bedroom, but it does signal that the property has been cared for, which helps buyers feel confident. It's also one of the few things about a sale that's fully in your control.</p>
<p>A professional <a href="{{service:one-off-cleaning}}">one-off clean</a> before your listing goes live is a straightforward way to get there without giving up your weekends.</p>
<h2>Declutter before you clean</h2>
<ul>
<li>Clear kitchen worktops down to the kettle and one or two other items</li>
<li>Remove most personal photos, fridge magnets and paperwork</li>
<li>Thin out wardrobes so the storage looks generous</li>
<li>Store or donate spare furniture to make rooms feel bigger</li>
<li>Tidy the loft, garage and under-stairs cupboard, because buyers do look</li>
<li>Clear toiletries from bathroom surfaces</li>
</ul>
<p>Decluttering also makes cleaning quicker and more thorough, because every surface is easy to reach.</p>
<h2>The rooms buyers look at most closely</h2>
<h3>Kitchen</h3>
<p>The kitchen gets the most scrutiny. Degrease cupboard doors and handles, clean the extractor hood, polish the sink and taps, and wipe out the fridge and cupboards, as buyers will open them. A dirty oven is a common turn-off, so clean it inside, including the glass door. Our <a href="{{guide:kitchen-deep-clean-checklist}}">kitchen deep clean checklist</a> covers everything step by step.</p>
<h3>Bathrooms</h3>
<p>Descale taps, shower heads and screens until the glass is clear, scrub the grout and replace any silicone that's stained black. Fresh towels and a clean bath mat finish the room off. In a hard water area, limescale is the first thing to tackle; see our guide to <a href="{{guide:hard-water-limescale-east-yorkshire}}">removing limescale</a>.</p>
<h3>Entrance and hallway</h3>
<p>First impressions start at the front door. Clean the door, letterbox, house number and step, sweep the path and put down a fresh doormat. Inside, wipe the skirting boards, banisters and light switches.</p>
<h3>Living room and bedrooms</h3>
<p>Clean the windows inside and out so rooms look brighter, dust light fittings and shelves, hoover under furniture and make the beds neatly. Tired carpets can look very different after a professional clean.</p>
<h2>How to get rid of smells before viewings</h2>
<p>Smells are the hardest thing to hide, and heavy air fresheners or strong candles can make buyers suspect you're covering something up. Tackle the source instead:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pets:</strong> wash pet bedding, clean carpets and sofas, and empty litter trays before each viewing. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:cleaning-with-pets}}">cleaning a home with pets</a> has more on odours.</li>
<li><strong>Cooking:</strong> clean the extractor filters and oven, and avoid strong-smelling meals the night before a viewing.</li>
<li><strong>Damp and mustiness:</strong> clean any mould, ventilate daily and run a dehumidifier. If it keeps coming back, read our guide to <a href="{{guide:damp-and-mould-in-older-homes}}">damp and mould in older homes</a>, as a buyer's surveyor is likely to spot it anyway.</li>
<li><strong>Bins and drains:</strong> wash the bins, clear drains and plugholes, and take rubbish out before buyers arrive.</li>
<li><strong>Smoke:</strong> wash walls and paintwork, clean curtains and soft furnishings, and air the house thoroughly.</li>
</ul>
<h2>When to clean: timing around photos and viewings</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Two to three weeks before listing:</strong> declutter, make small repairs and touch up paintwork.</li>
<li><strong>A few days before the photos:</strong> deep clean the whole house, including the windows, and have carpets cleaned so they have time to dry.</li>
<li><strong>The morning of the photos:</strong> clear surfaces, open curtains and blinds, switch on lights and hide bins, cables and toiletries.</li>
<li><strong>Throughout the sale:</strong> keep a weekly routine going and do a quick tidy before each viewing.</li>
</ol>
<p>Booking <a href="{{service:carpet-upholstery-cleaning}}">carpet and upholstery cleaning</a> alongside your main clean freshens walkways and lifts odours from sofas and rugs before the camera comes out.</p>
<div class="cc-callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Walk round your home as if you were a buyer, opening cupboards and looking up at the ceilings. List everything that catches your eye and work through it before the photographer arrives.</p></div>
<h2>A quick cleaning routine before every viewing</h2>
<ol>
<li>Open the windows for ten minutes to freshen the air</li>
<li>Clear the kitchen worktops and load the dishwasher</li>
<li>Wipe the sink, taps and hob</li>
<li>Wipe the bathroom basin, toilet and mirror, and hang fresh towels</li>
<li>Make the beds and plump the cushions</li>
<li>Hoover the main walkways</li>
<li>Empty all the bins and take the rubbish outside</li>
<li>Put away shoes, coats and children's toys</li>
<li>Switch on lights and open the curtains</li>
</ol>
<p>Once the house has had a proper clean, this routine takes around half an hour. Share it out across the household and it's quicker still.</p>
<h2>Cleaning when you move out</h2>
<p>Once you've sold, it's good practice to leave the house clean for the new owners, and most buyers will expect to find it in the condition they saw at the viewings. Plan it into your move using our <a href="{{guide:moving-house-cleaning-timeline}}">week-by-week moving house cleaning timeline</a>, and if you're buying too, think about cleaning your new home before you unpack.</p>
<h2>Getting your home ready to sell</h2>
<p>From terraces in Hull to family homes in <a href="{{area:anlaby-willerby-kirk-ella}}">Willerby and Kirk Ella</a> and period properties in <a href="{{area:beverley}}">Beverley</a>, our team helps sellers present their homes at their best. A <a href="{{service:one-off-cleaning}}">one-off clean</a> before the photos covers the kitchen, bathrooms, skirting boards, interior windows and everything in between, and a full <a href="{{service:deep-cleaning}}">deep clean</a> is there for homes that need more attention.</p>
<p>We agree a fixed quote before work starts, our cleaners bring all their own equipment, and we're open seven days a week to fit around your estate agent's schedule. <a href="{{page:contact}}">Get in touch</a> to book a clean before your listing goes live.</p>
